<p>Right, I forgot to add what's happening here. If you've figured it out already, good for you, but I just want to clear a couple things up.</p>
<p>What's happening here is, the Foundation discovered these documents and files. It's not stated where they got it, or how they even know of it, but they just found it.</p>
<p>When the Overseers heard about this, they send out an MTF to administer amnestics to the personnel involved in its discovery and confiscate the files. They log the files into the database in the form of a fake dangerous SCP and transfer the actual documents off to Site-01.</p>
<p>The fake skip is basically just a worn-out notepad with gibberish and doodles drawn in but its non-anomalous. They added security protocols to this fake skip so that, if one decides to steal or use it in unauthorized testing, they will know about it.</p>
<p>All in all, since the real SCP isn't anomalous to begin with, it's held in Site-01 as the only SCP to be brought into a Protected Site.</p>
